WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.720
- [George] Tesla is going to win
Level 5, they really are.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.970
- [Lex] So, let's talk about it.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:16.970
So, you're focused on
Level 2, currently, currently.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.340
- [George] We're going to be one to
two years behind Tesla,

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.310
getting to Level 5.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.164
- Okay.

00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:22.997
(laughs)

00:00:22.997 --> 00:00:24.070
- [George] We're
Android, right, we're Android.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:24.903
- You're Android.

00:00:24.903 --> 00:00:26.420
- [George] I'm just
saying, once Tesla gets it,

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.532
we're one to two years behind.

00:00:27.532 --> 00:00:29.672
I'm not making any timeline
on when Tesla's gonna get it.

00:00:29.672 --> 00:00:30.540
- That's right, you did.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.373
That was brilliant.

00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:36.030
So, what do you think about
this. Most Level 4 companies

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:41.243
are kinda just doing their usual,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.000
safety driver, doing
full autonomy kinda testing.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.080
And then Tesla does, basically trying

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.770
to go from lane keeping to full autonomy.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.030
What do you think about that approach?

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.600
How successful would it be?

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.810
- It's a ton better
approach, because Tesla

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.420
is gathering data on a
scale that none of them are.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.720
They're putting real users
behind the wheel of the cars.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.443
It's, I think, the only
strategy that works.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.650
The incremental.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.160
- Well, so there's a few
components to Tesla's approach,

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.320
that's more than just incremental.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.590
You spoke with... One is software,

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.110
so, over the air software updates.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.040
- [George] Necessity.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.620
I mean Waymo and Cruise have those too.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:23.790
Those aren't.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.010
But those differentiate
them from the automakers.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.150
- Right, no lane keeping systems have,

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.980
no cars with lane keeping
systems have that except Tesla.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:31.930
- [George] Yep.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:35.970
And the other one is the
data, the other direction,

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.060
which is the ability to query the data.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.700
I don't think they're actually collecting

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.710
as much data as people think.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.333
But the ability to turn on
collection, and turn it off.

